 r←{x}RefLog y;space;folder;rc;more;branch;buff;restrictFlag;cmd
⍝ Execute Git's "reflog" command.\\
⍝ Returns a matrix with zero or more rows and these columns:\\
⍝ * `[1]` Hash
⍝ * `[2]` Symbolic pointer: `HEAD`, or the branch in case one was specified
⍝ * `[3]` Command
⍝ * `[4]` Message, either from the user of from Git\\
⍝ `y` is either `restrictFlag` or `(restrictFlag branch)`:\\
⍝ * `restrictFlag` defaults to 0 when empty; this lists all entries.
⍝   If this is 1 then only the entries up to the last checkout are listed.
⍝ * `branch` defaults to an empty vector, meaning the reflog of `HEAD`.\\
⍝ For what `x` can actually be see `EstablishProject`.\\
 r←⍬
 x←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}'x'
 :If 0=≢y
     (restrictFlag branch)←0 ''
 :ElseIf 1<≢y
     (restrictFlag branch)←(⊃,⊃y)(∊1↓y)
 :Else
     (restrictFlag branch)←(⊃,y)''
 :EndIf
 'Restriction flag must be a Boolean'U.Assert(⊂restrictFlag)∊0 1
 (space folder)←EstablishProject x
 cmd←'reflog',{0=≢⍵:'' ⋄ ' "',⍵,'"'}branch
 (rc more buff)←folder U.RunGitCommand cmd
 :If 0≠rc
 :AndIf ∨/'unknown revision'⍷∊more
     ('There is no branch "',branch,'" in this project')U.Assert 0
 :EndIf
 ('RefLog crashed with RC=',(⍕rc),'; ',∊more)U.Assert 0=rc
 r←↑3{⍺{(⍺↑⍵),{⍺,' ',⍵}/⍺↓⍵}' '(≠⊆⊢)⍵}¨buff
 :If restrictFlag
 :AndIf 0<≢r
     r←(¯1+r[;3]⍳⊂'checkout:')↑r
 :EndIf
⍝Done
